window.EN={"1":"Having crossed the great Thracia River, Leif's army makes straight for Munster in one push.","2":"Meanwhile in Munster, in response to the movements of Leif's army, citizens were attempting to escape one after another,","3":"and between the \"Magi Squad\" led by Ced, supporting them, and the Munster army, trying to stop them,","4":"fierce fighting was being waged day after day.","5":"Lord Ced, even our last hideout has been found by Raydrik.","6":"At this rate, the children...","7":"It would be good if I could take them and flee,","8":"but then there would be no one to command the revolt. If only there were someone I could trust...","9":"Shall I take on that duty?","10":"Who's there!... Who are you!?","11":"Merely a passerby, but I have heard what you were saying.","12":"If you wish to evacuate the children outside the castle, shall I help?","13":"Or can you not trust me?","14":"No... You are wrapped in a gentle wind.","15":"You do not seem to be a person of ill will, but who are you? From your appearance, a priest of the Empire...","16":"Regrettably, I can say nothing now. But if you will trust me, I will protect the children.","17":"I understand... Then, I ask it of you. And one more thing: this sword, please...","18":"A sword...?","19":"This is the \"Bragi Sword.\" I had heard it was within the castle, but you did well to get hold of it.","20":"Yes. Raydrik is protected by the \"Loptr Sword.\"","21":"Without this sword, he cannot be defeated.","22":"I see... And what would you have me do?","23":"This sword can only be used by a swordsman who has the blood of the crusaders.","24":"I want you to entrust it to Prince Leif of the Liberation Army, who is said to be heading for this castle.","25":"Understood. If I am able to meet him, I will hand it over.","26":"Thank you.","27":"Ah... Father! At least your name...","28":"Forgive my rudeness. I am Saias, of Velthomer...","29":"What, there are people fleeing from this Munster!?","30":"Sir. It appears the Magi Squad's people are secretly helping children escape.","31":"Curse them. Children are precious goods that must be offered up to the Empire...","32":"Farden, while we're at it, dispose of the fleeing children.","33":"Show the citizens remaining in the castle what happens if they run.","34":"Leave it to me.","35":"Lord Raydrik, I heard you summoned me...","36":"Alphand. You are to guard the gate of Munster Castle.","37":"I hear the whelp of Leonster is marching on Munster.","38":"And the Magi Squad lot inside the castle are not to be underestimated either.","39":"In any case, the gate must not be handed to them. Understood!","40":"Yes. Then I shall take up the defense of the gate at once.","41":"Munster at last.","42":"...It seems that in Munster, skirmishes continue between the Magi Squad and the Munster army.","43":"Though its power has declined from before, the Munster army is still strong.","44":"Without the Magi Squad's help, taking it will be impossible.","45":"...Oh? There is some movement in that Munster...","46":"It appears children have come fleeing out.","47":"What!? Let's rescue them at once!","48":"Coulter, how do things look in Munster?","49":"No major movement for the moment. But if our information is correct, there should be a major movement within days.","50":"We judge that chance, and in one stroke...","51":"But to drag the citizens into it for that...","52":"If Munster is freed from the Empire's hands, that in itself is to our country's benefit.","53":"Is that not good enough as it is?","54":"Well... but this is His Majesty's order...","55":"...I will try somehow to persuade my father.","56":"Lady Altena is too soft... Now is the best chance to get hold of Munster.","57":"His Majesty is soft on Her Highness the princess too, but I hear that on this matter even he will not lend an ear.","58":"Here, it is best simply to act according to His Majesty's order...","59":"You called, Lord Alphand?","60":"Hey, I can't find my tome. Go look for it.","61":"What, again...","62":"What? Did you say something just now?","63":"No, nothing... So, which tome is it this time?","64":"...The tome called Poison. Without it I can't attack distant enemies.","65":"Understood. I will go and look, so please wait.","66":"I hope it's somewhere easier to find than last time...","67":"Lord Alphand, I've found it!","68":"Really! Well done!","69":"Just you watch, rebels. I'll teach you the terror of this magic!","70":"Before that, at least put your tomes away properly...","71":"Mm! It seems there has been a major movement in Munster.","72":"It is our chance! We will now attack into Munster.","73":"Wait! If we attack into Munster now, even the citizens will be caught up in it.","74":"I will somehow persuade them to surrender...","75":"This is the order of His Majesty the King! Even Your Highness the princess must not interfere!","76":"I am the commander!","77":"This unit is my unit! And it is His Majesty's order that the attack must not be eased, whatever Lady Altena may say!","78":"Wha...","79":"...If it displeases you, you may stay here and watch.","80":"All troops, move out!","81":"Coulter! Wait! Coulter!","82":"I must somehow persuade Father and have the attack called off...","83":"Mmh! Who are you!","84":"I am Ced of the Magi Squad. Except for one part of the castle interior, Munster has been secured by our Magi Squad.","85":"If you surrender to us quietly, your lives are guaranteed...","86":"Don't mock me! Who would believe such nonsense!","87":"You are...? The hero Ced!?","88":"Prince Leif!?... You've finally come!","89":"I'm sorry to be so late.","90":"I haven't even thanked you yet for saving me, Prince Ced...","91":"Never mind that, but how do you know I'm a prince? Ah, did you hear it from Karin?","92":"Yes. I heard that though by rights you ought to return to your country before anything else,","93":"you stayed, having no choice, in order to protect the people of Munster.","94":"All because I was so useless. I'm truly sorry.","95":"It's nothing for you to apologize for, Prince.","96":"I meant to liberate it sooner,","97":"but even with this Forseti, I could not break Raydrik's \"Loptr Sword.\"","98":"Because of that, I lost many whom I should have saved.","99":"It is all because my strength fell short... It is no responsibility of yours, Prince.","100":"No... I envy you.","101":"That power for which you are called a hero is truly that of the Crusader Ced. I have no such power.","102":"I... am different from Lord Seliph and from you.","103":"I... am not a crusader...","104":"Prince Leif...? What on earth are you saying!?","105":"What exactly is a crusader? Simply one who inherits a holy weapon? Surely not.","106":"Once, this Jugdral, for a span of several hundred years,","107":"was ruled by an evil empire that worshipped the dark god Loptous.","108":"Those who rescued the people from that rule: those are the heroes who were called crusaders.","109":"Prince Leif, you have already been waging that battle for a year. It must have been a painful and difficult fight.","110":"But to save the people, you have fought this holy war, Prince.","111":"I don't think Lord Seliph or I am any greater than you.","112":"You, who were the youngest, grew up amid the greatest hardship and have fought longer than anyone.","113":"If that is not a crusader, then what on earth is!","114":"Prince Leif, have more confidence!","115":"You are, without a doubt, a crusader who carries on the will of Nova!","116":"Prince Ced... thank you.","117":"Meeting Lord Seliph and you, I was overwhelmed by the difference in stature, and so I lost my nerve...","118":"Perhaps I'm still a child.","119":"That's not so. Or are you saying I was saved by a child?","120":"Ah... no, I didn't mean...","121":"Hahaha... No, this was no time for joking.","122":"About Raydrik: we managed to corner him in one part of the castle.","123":"But he has taken children hostage and barricaded himself in.","124":"The Magi Squad has its hands full securing the town, and has no strength left over to fight.","125":"Prince Leif, you'll lend me your strength?","126":"Of course! Raydrik is a hated enemy to me as well.","127":"If I can fight alongside you, nothing could make me happier.","128":"I see. Just what I'd expect of the prince of Leonster. I'm looking forward to it too!","129":"Father!? You, with the children?","130":"Yes. Sir Ced of the Magi Squad asked it of me.","131":"Thank you for coming to our aid.","132":"No, I'm the one who should thank you. Thank you for saving the children.","133":"Leave the rest to us, and please withdraw to a safe place, Father.","134":"Yes... This is the first time we meet, but you are Prince Leif, are you not?","135":"Yes, I am, but how did you...","136":"As I thought... Then please accept this sword.","137":"It is called the \"Bragi Sword,\" and it is indispensable for fighting Raydrik.","138":"This? To me...","139":"Yes. Sir Ced asked that it be given to you...","140":"This sword is a holy sword that only one with the blood of the crusaders can wield.","141":"But as Sir Ced cannot use swords, he must have entrusted it to you.","142":"A holy sword... This is the holy sword of Bragi!...","143":"I understand. If it is a sword for defeating Raydrik, I could ask for nothing better.","144":"Father, I am grateful.","145":"In the coming battle, please do not forget it... Well then, Sir Leif, until later...","146":"What, the Magi Squad has been wiped out?","147":"Having lost its leader, the Magi Squad collapsed entirely, and it seems Munster has been seized by Thracia.","148":"Without the Magi Squad's cooperation, our taking of Munster is impossible...","149":"Prince Leif, we have managed to reach the castle gate, but what now?","150":"I'm told the Magi Squad has secured the town, so there's no worry there,","151":"but Raydrik seems to have taken children hostage and fled into the palace. A coward as always.","152":"I am told Raydrik is protected by a cursed sword of Loptr. If that is true, we must devise a countermeasure.","153":"That's all right. A priest who escaped from inside the castle entrusted me with a sword.","154":"It seems to be what's called the \"Bragi Sword,\" the counterpart of the \"Loptr Sword.\"","155":"He said that with that sword, one can fight evenly even against the Loptr Sword.","156":"Hmm... That is good news.","157":"Then in the coming battle, be sure that you yourself equip the \"Bragi Sword,\" Prince!","158":"Lord Leif, is it not reckless to advance as things stand?","159":"Then what would you have me do, August?","160":"Think it over once more.","161":"Whether you have forgotten something important, whether you have lost something important.","162":"It will not be too late to advance into the castle after that.","163":"You need not worry about that. I have been entrusted with this sword by Sir Ced.","164":"Sir Leif, with the blood of the crusaders, should be able to wield it.","165":"What sword is this?","166":"What is called the \"Bragi Sword,\" the counterpart of the \"Loptr Sword.\"","167":"With this sword, one should be able to fight evenly even against the Loptr Sword.","168":"The holy sword of Bragi... What a magnificent sword! Father Saias, I am grateful.","169":"Your thanks should go to Sir Ced. I was merely keeping it.","170":"Yes...","171":"By the way, Father, what will you do now?","172":"I no longer have a place to return to. Only... there is one thing I have left undone.","173":"To receive the oracle for it, I intend to go to the Tower of Bragi.","174":"...Even if I ask your circumstances, you won't tell me, will you?","175":"No. Not yet, nothing...","176":"Father, if your journey is not urgent, would you lend us your strength just a little longer?","177":"We need you.","178":"I am sorry, but I cannot bring myself to do so now.","179":"Sir Leif, I shall pray for your fortune in battle from the distant Tower of Bragi.","180":"Then, I take my leave...","181":"To defeat Raydrik...?","182":"......Very well.","183":"If this, too, is God's will, it cannot be helped.","184":"I shall remain a little while longer.","185":"Everyone in the Liberation Army, please save us from the Empire!","186":"This is a vulnerary. I hope it can be of use to you all...","187":"So you're attacking Munster? Then take this holy water with you.","188":"Munster is full of Loptr monks. One can't be too careful.","189":"I wonder if the people who fled Munster are all right. I hope they get away safely.","190":"You, I'll give you this Physic staff, so help them if they get into danger.","191":"You must not underestimate Raydrik.","192":"That man has the Loptr Church on his side, and holds a terrible sword called the \"Loptr Sword.\"","193":"Fight against that sword the ordinary way, and you have no chance of winning.","194":"In the past there was a sword in the castle that could counter it...","195":"but I hear that, too, has now been lost somewhere.","196":"The power of darkness is fearsome... for it has the power to turn all living things to stone.","197":"But according to tradition, the darkness also has the power to restore those turned to stone.","198":"Though for that, it seems a staff with a special power is needed.","199":"Heh heh heh... Sorry, but you'll have to die.","200":"...Glory... to Thracia! ...gah!","201":"...It won't go like this next time. I'll make you regret sparing me, without fail!","202":"Wh-what, they've come even to a place like this...","203":"Gwah... I don't... want to die... yet...","204":"You'll spare me! I see, I'm grateful...","205":"Rebels! I'll teach you the strength of our Munster army!","206":"Ugh... It wasn't supposed to go like this...","207":"Sorry, I owe you..."};
